second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is Arthur Mellersh's military rank?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 167, \"text\": \"As the sun dipped into the horizon, casting a warm orange glow over the bustling streets of London, Lieutenant Arthur Mellersh made his way through the crowded tavern.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 168, \"end\": 263, \"text\": \"The year was 1837, and the British Royal Navy was abuzz with the latest news from the colonies.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 264, \"end\": 475, \"text\": \"Mellersh, a dashing young officer with a keen mind and a quick wit, had just received a cryptic message from an old acquaintance, hinting at a mysterious meeting that would change the course of his life forever.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 476, \"end\": 594, \"text\": \"As he pushed open the door, a warm fire crackled in the hearth, and the murmur of hushed conversations filled the air.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 595, \"end\": 676, \"text\": \"Mellersh's eyes scanned the room, searching for the familiar face of his contact.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 677, \"end\": 807, \"text\": \"That was when he spotted her – a striking woman with piercing green eyes and raven-black hair, sipping a cup of tea in the corner.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 808, \"end\": 907, \"text\": \"She beckoned him over with a discreet nod, and Mellersh made his way through the throng of patrons.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 908, \"end\": 980, \"text\": \"\\\"Captain Orlova,\\\" he said, bowing slightly as he took a seat beside her.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 981, \"end\": 1026, \"text\": \"\\\"I must admit, I'm intrigued by your message.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1027, \"end\": 1065, \"text\": \"What news do you bring from the east?\\\"\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1066, \"end\": 1143, \"text\": \"Captain Orlova, a seasoned veteran of the Russian Navy, smiled enigmatically.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1144, \"end\": 1232, \"text\": \"\\\"Let us just say, Lieutenant, that the winds of change are blowing across the continent.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1233, \"end\": 1377, \"text\": \"The Soviet Union, as you know, is still in its infancy, but its leaders are already making bold moves to secure their place on the world stage.\\\"\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1378, \"end\": 1410, \"text\": \"Mellersh's curiosity was piqued.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1411, \"end\": 1454, \"text\": \"\\\"Go on,\\\" he urged, his eyes locked on hers.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1455, \"end\": 1506, \"text\": \"Orlova leaned in, her voice barely above a whisper.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1507, \"end\": 1640, \"text\": \"\\\"I have it on good authority that the Soviet high command is seeking to forge alliances with key military leaders from across Europe.\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1641, \"end\": 1731, \"text\": \"And I believe you, Lieutenant Mellersh, have a crucial role to play in this grand design.\\\"\"}, \"D1S19\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1732, \"end\": 1900, \"text\": \"As Mellersh listened, entranced, Orlova outlined a plan that would take him from the familiar waters of the Royal Navy to the uncharted territories of the Soviet Union.\"}, \"D1S20\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1901, \"end\": 2040, \"text\": \"It was a journey that would test his mettle, challenge his loyalties, and ultimately, propel him to the highest echelons of military power.\"}, \"D1S21\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2041, \"end\": 2173, \"text\": \"The fire crackled, and the patrons of the tavern laughed and chatted, oblivious to the subtle machinations unfolding in their midst.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 19, \"text\": \"**Arthur Mellersh**\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 21, \"end\": 110, \"text\": \"Arthur Mellersh was a British Royal Navy officer who held the rank of lieutenant in 1837.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 111, \"end\": 136, \"text\": \"**Early Life and Career**\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 138, \"end\": 209, \"text\": \"There is limited information available on Arthur Mellersh's early life.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 210, \"end\": 311, \"text\": \"However, it is known that he joined the Royal Navy and rose through the ranks to become a lieutenant.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 312, \"end\": 334, \"text\": \"**Rank of Lieutenant**\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 336, \"end\": 466, \"text\": \"A lieutenant is a junior commissioned officer rank in the Royal Navy, ranking above sub-lieutenant and below lieutenant commander.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 467, \"end\": 565, \"text\": \"The rank of lieutenant is equivalent to the rank of captain in the British Army and Royal Marines.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 566, \"end\": 586, \"text\": \"**Evidence of Rank**\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 588, \"end\": 684, \"text\": \"According to the Navy List of 1837, Arthur Mellersh is listed as a lieutenant in the Royal Navy.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 685, \"end\": 870, \"text\": \"[1] This publication, which was published quarterly by the British Admiralty, provided a comprehensive list of all officers in the Royal Navy, including their rank and ship assignments.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 871, \"end\": 998, \"text\": \"Additionally, Mellersh's service record, held at the National Archives in Kew, London, confirms his rank as lieutenant in 1837.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 999, \"end\": 1002, \"text\": \"[2]\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1004, \"end\": 1018, \"text\": \"**References**\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1020, \"end\": 1044, \"text\": \"[1] The Navy List, 1837.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1045, \"end\": 1065, \"text\": \"London: John Murray.\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1066, \"end\": 1101, \"text\": \"[2] National Archives, Kew, London.\"}, \"D2S18\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1102, \"end\": 1136, \"text\": \"ADM 196\\\\/1\\\\/144, Mellersh, Arthur.\"}, \"D2S19\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1137, \"end\": 1152, \"text\": \"Service Record.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Arthur Mellersh\", \"scope\": \"military rank\", \"claim\": \"Arthur Mellersh held the military rank of Lieutenant.\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant\", \"quote\": \"As the sun dipped into the horizon, casting a warm orange glow over the bustling streets of London, Lieutenant Arthur Mellersh made his way through the crowded tavern. The year was 1837, and the British Royal Navy was abuzz with the latest news from the colonies. Mellersh, a dashing young officer with a keen mind and a quick wit, had just received a cryptic message from an old acquaintance, hinting at a mysterious meeting that would change the course of his life forever. As he pushed open the door, a warm fire crackled in the hearth, and the murmur of hushed conversations filled the air. Mellersh's eyes scanned the room, searching for the familiar face of his contact. That was when he spotted her – a striking woman with piercing green eyes and raven-black hair, sipping a cup of tea in the corner. She beckoned him over with a discreet nod, and Mellersh made his way through the throng of patrons. \\\"Captain Orlova,\\\" he said, bowing slightly as he took a seat beside her. \\\"I must admit, I'm intrigued by your message. What news do you bring from the east?\\\" Captain Orlova, a seasoned veteran of the Russian Navy, smiled enigmatically. \\\"Let us just say, Lieutenant, that the winds of change are blowing across the continent.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Lieutenant\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (equivalent to Captain in British Army/Royal Marines)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (confirmed by Navy List of 1837)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (confirmed by National Archives service record)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C4\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (junior commissioned officer, above sub-lieutenant)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C5\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (held in 1837)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C6\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (Royal Navy rank)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C7\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (ranked below lieutenant commander)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C8\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (as per Navy List 1837)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C9\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (as per National Archives ADM 196/1/144)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C10\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (British Royal Navy officer)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C11\", \"answer\": \"Lieutenant (junior commissioned officer rank)\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}]}"
